{:edb/db-before-t 2757 :edb/db-after-t 2758 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536070 50 #inst "2026-10-09T14:17:20.693Z" 13194139536070 true] [17592186124429 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382141 13194139536070 true] [17592186124430 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382120 13194139536070 true] [17592186124431 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382127 13194139536070 true] [17592186124431 1020 #edb/ref 17592186382134 13194139536070 true] [17592186124793 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536070 true] [17592186124793 1100 "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139536070 true] [17592186124793 1100 "Consider the matrices given below. Find $dim(Null(A)) + dim(Null(B)) + dim(Null(C))$.\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139536070 false] [17592186124793 1145 "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $4$th columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $4$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\t